# CA-001 — Astrid doesn't yet have a culture where creatives thrive

**Applies to:** [A Shared Creative Endeavor](../pillars/shared-endeavour.md) (primary) · **Assessment:** Open; prior Banodoco competitions, but no established Astrid-specific program/outcome audit.

## Desired state

People have compelling reasons to attempt work beyond their current abilities: artistic challenges, collaboration, critiques, showcases and high standards that encourage originality and growth.

## Current state

Astrid builds on the existing Banodoco community, which has run art competitions including the [Arca Gidan Prize](https://arcagidan.com/). But **Astrid has not yet established a community centred on this tool and its artistic mission**, with a repeatable culture of challenges, critique and collective artistic growth. Earlier competitions provide experience and a starting point, not evidence that this new culture already exists.

## Gap

Astrid doesn't yet have a thriving culture of creatives challenging, inspiring and helping one another reach beyond their current abilities. Challenges, critique, showcases and recognition should be judged by the creative work and growth they enable, not activity counts alone.

## Closure evidence

Run a bounded challenge with clear artistic intent and fair participation; document artists' goals, feedback, completed work and whether it enabled more ambitious efforts. Incorporate genuine creator assessment, including negative findings and barriers.

## Sources and reassessment

[Collective Ambition principle](../pillars/shared-endeavour.md). Any community program needs an accountable owner, accessibility considerations and its own execution/assessment plan. No such plan is authorized by this gap.
